"""Model label -> this app's species identity, for
`app/dao/bird_classifier.py`'s photo classifier.

The model (`dennisjooo/Birds-Classifier-EfficientNetB2`, see
`docs/features/bird-id.md`) outputs one of 525 Kaggle-dataset labels
(e.g. "NORTHERN CARDINAL") -- not an eBird species code or scientific name.
This crosswalk was built by normalized-matching each label against a live
`GET /ref/taxonomy/ebird` pull (17,891 species), then hand-verifying every
label that didn't match outright: some were Kaggle-dataset typos
("BLACKBURNIAM WARBLER"), some were outdated common names now split into
separate species by current taxonomy ("BARN OWL" -> American Barn Owl, not
the Old World's Western Barn Owl; "ROCK DOVE" -> Rock Pigeon), and some are
simply not real species at all (Kaggle labels like "ALBATROSS" or "CROW"
name a whole family/genus, with no single matching scientific name).

Carries the full identity (scientific/common name + eBird species code),
not just scientific_name -- there's no local species-lookup table yet (see
`species_repo.py` in bird-info.md's plan), so this is self-contained rather
than needing a second lookup per classification.

**Deliberately incomplete** -- 95 of 525 labels have no entry.
`bird_classifier.py` must treat a label with no crosswalk entry as "skip
this candidate," not an error. Known gaps: generic group labels
("ALBATROSS", "COCKATOO", "CROW", "TAILORBIRD", ...) that were never going
to resolve to one species, plus a long tail of non-North-American species
whose Kaggle label didn't cleanly match current eBird nomenclature and
weren't worth individually chasing for a NC-focused beta app. Extend this
by hand if a specific gap turns out to matter.
"""

